    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so i just updated our A records for the main client site but it's still pointing to the old server on my end even though i cleared my local cache. why does it take so long for dns changes to actually show up everywhere?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This delay is due to a process called DNS propagation. Once you update the A records, DNS resolvers across the internet need time to catch up and update their cached information. This process can take anywhere from a few minutes to up to 48 hours depending on the Time To Live (TTL) settings of your previous records. For immediate testing, you can use online DNS checker tools to see where the new records are resolving from.",
