    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "makes sense. so the TTL is basically just telling the servers how long to hold onto the old info before checking again? is there any way to actually speed up the propagation once it's already started, or are we just stuck waiting?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That's correct; TTL dictates how long resolvers should cache the old IP before querying for an update. Unfortunately, once propagation starts, there is no technical switch to force all global servers to update instantly. However, reducing the TTL *before* making the change is the best preventative measure for future updates. For the current situation, patience is key as you wait for the remaining caches to expire.",
      "source": "target",
